**Step 6 | Records branch (one commit) and the catch-up copies.** (a) Re-scan the C-numbers (free, else STOP). (b) The C-entries, BACKLOG rows and history entry are the FIXED TEXT PARTS `<CE-*>`, `<CL-*>`, `<BL-*>`, `<HI-*>`; every figure MEASURED or RELAYED with source; each entry names what is NOT settled. (c) **Catch-up STATUS copies (three):** `2026-10-29_B884_STATUS.md`, `2026-10-29_B886_STATUS.md`, `2026-10-29_B896_STATUS.md`, copied unchanged from the project `Briefs/`, each only if its last line is its own final line (`RECORDS COMMITTED:`, `READY FOR QA:`, `VERDICT:`), its sha256 equals Step 2's and its mtime is older than 10 minutes; `git check-ignore` rc 1 each; `/usr/bin/grep -c -i 'HP Restricted'` (expected 4, 0, 0; control 1 on a planted line); report e-mail shapes, non-ASCII and name-class hits (report, never edit a copy). **Never copy the B885, B891, B900, B901, B903 STATUS files or any `*_evidence/` folder.** (d) Closing checks as B884 (gitleaks per path with a firing canary; name and key-value scans over added lines; `git diff --stat origin/main..records/b907` lists the three files and three copies and nothing else; 0 deleted lines in the three files except none; the new C-numbers repeat nowhere; "main is green" is written nowhere). One commit (message names B907, PR #239, the keys, no person's name, no card id), never amend, push plainly, read `ls-remote` after the last push.
**Step 7 | STATUS.** Sections: Questions, BLUF, Step 0, PINS, PRIOR WORK, Facts re-measured, HELD, Jira (before/after, searches, texts' sha256, keys, comment ids, read-back), Records (C-numbers, rows, history, catch-up list with sha256), Closing checks, Gate check, Landing, NOT TESTED, FOR TUESDAY, Corrections, files and trees left. **FOR TUESDAY:** (1) the keys made and the comment ids; (2) T04 created or HELD and why; (3) the B884 history line 4 correction; (4) the ruling entry's number (the build seat for HPSMPOC-383 cites it); (5) the catch-up scan hits; (6) the gate check's printed result.
**Step 8 | GATE CHECK, then landing.** **No landing while any gate STATUS file of 2026-10-29 has no final line.** Run this check (a) at Step 0 for the record, (b) immediately before you push, and (c) immediately before you open the PR and again before you merge; a landing that moves main mid-gate forces the gate to re-run. The check, as one `bash -c` program printing one row per file: for every `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/tuesday/briefs/<today>_B<n>_SEAT-G*hpsmpoc*.md` (skip `.pre-*`) the file `Briefs/<today>_B<n>_STATUS.md` must exist and its last non-empty line must begin `VERDICT:`, `STOPPED:` or `BLOCKED:`; AND every `Briefs/<today>_B*_STATUS.md` whose first line contains `GATE` (case-insensitive) must end the same way; AND no pane named `Datasec/HPSM-POC-G*` is live. **Drafter's run 20:0x: B896 FINAL, B900 FINAL, B901 FINAL; B903 (a builder, first line `PROGRESS`) is not a gate; panes: H55 only. Controls the seat re-runs: a scratch copy of the B896 STATUS with its last line removed prints NOT-FINAL; the B903 STATUS last line begins `WORKING:`.** If ANY row is NOT-FINAL or a gate pane is live: do every other step, push `records/b907`, open NO PR, and end with `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY gate <file or pane> has no final line; records/b907 @ <sha40> pushed; Jira: <keys, comment ids>`. If clear: open ONE PR for `records/b907` (title names B907, PR #239 and the keys; no person's name, no card id), wait until every check on its head is complete and success and the code-scanning analyses for the PR ref are complete with 0 open alerts (never bypass the ruleset, never dismiss an alert), re-run the gate check, and land by MERGE COMMIT with `--match-head-commit <your head>` (first line "Merge pull request #<n> from datasecau/records/b907"; precedents B871 PR #149, B880 PR #150, B884 PR #151). If the repository refuses the merge, or needs an approval or bypass you lack: STOP with the PR number and the one refusal; never force, never change a ruleset. Read back: records `main` = the merge sha; main contains `{C-RULING}`, `{C-LAND}` (control: `C-224` still present) and the B907 rows.
**Last line of the STATUS FILE, exactly one of:** `RECORDS COMMITTED: records/b907 @ <sha40> | PR #<n> merged as <sha40> | 2 C-entries (<C-RULING>, <C-LAND>), <n> BACKLOG rows, 1 history entry, 3 catch-up files | Jira: <n> tickets (<keys>), <n> label adds, 2 comments (HPSMPOC-363 = <id>, HPSMPOC-364 = <id>), 0 transitions, 0 edits | SKIPS <...> HELD <...> | PRIOR WORK section present`; `RECORDS PUSHED: records/b907 @ <sha40> | PR not landed (<reason>) | ...`; `RECORDS DONE: nothing to push (<reason>) | Jira: ...`; or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` with ONE question.

