- `<R-0>` = BLUF: PR #239 (merged 2026-10-29 16:52:56 AEDT as squash 885692995df9f650b80dd4827fa0827349a7f619) added the rule rule_module_call_bindings to the infra security tests. Its gate (round 1 of 2, go with findings, nothing above a Note) probed the rule and found the limits below. The landed template is right and nothing is red today; each item is a guard that would not see, or would wrongly refuse, a FUTURE edit. Test-only: no product byte changes. Nothing is deployed.
- `<R-1>` = Finding B896-1 (Note, a design limit of the rule): the rule evaluates variables.prefix for dev, uat and demo with the file's own evaluated() helper (line {L-EVAL}) inside prefix_problem (line {L-PREFIX}), and that helper reads format and parameter references but not concat or toLower. A prefix written as [concat('hpsmpoc-', parameters('environmentName'))] or [toLower(format('hpsmpoc-{0}', parameters('environmentName')))] gives the same three texts, yet the rule reports that it cannot be read for every environment and the infra suite goes red; the older substring rule accepts both. The landed template writes the prefix as an interpolation that compiles to format, so only a deliberate hand edit reaches this. The refusal is loud and fail-safe. The gate wrote its own failure line ("red on a legitimate shape the ticket does not forbid") and it is met for these two shapes, so the grade may be raised.
- `<R-2>` = Finding B896-2 (Note, a residual wider than the PR text said): the rule does not require variables.names.keyVault to place variables('suffix') at all, and no rule reads variables.suffix. A name format of [format('kv-{0}', variables('prefix'))] and a variables.suffix typed as a constant both read clean on all 25 rules. Effect: a vault name without the unique suffix could collide at deploy (loud at deploy, not silent).
- `<R-3>` = Finding B896-3 (Note, a residual the PR text disclosed): the monitoring and identity module calls pass prefix: prefix (infra/main.bicep, the params lines {L-MON} and {L-IDN}) and no rule reads those two bindings; a constant typed there reads clean.
- `<R-5>` = Where: infra/tests/test_security_baseline.py (arm_value at line {L-ARM}, evaluated at line {L-EVAL}, prefix_problem at line {L-PREFIX}, rule_module_call_bindings at line {L-RULE}) and infra/main.bicep, read at main 885692995df9f650b80dd4827fa0827349a7f619 on 2026-10-29 {READ-TIME} AEDT. Recommendation (the gate's fix shapes): extend the evaluator to read concat and toLower, or record the refusal as intended; require names.keyVault to place variables('suffix') at its position and read the definition of variables.suffix; bind the monitoring and identity prefix to variables('prefix') in a row. Done when: a prefix written with concat or toLower reads no message (or the refusal is recorded as intended), the suffix and typed-prefix plants are each red under the rule while the landed template stays green, every existing row stays green, and no product byte changes.
